Kubernetes Services enable communication between various components within and outside of the application

Services helps us connect application(containers) together with other applications or users 

for ex: our application has groups of pods running various section
such as group of pod serving frontend loads to users, another group for runnin backend applications
third group connecting to an external data source

it is services that enables connectivity b/e these groups

thus services enables loose coupling b/w microservices in our application

a Kubernetes service is an object just like pods, replica sets, or deployments

one of its use is listen to a port on the node and forward requests on that port to a port on the pod running web application and this type of service is called node port service

service types
1) node port : service makes internal pod accessible on a port on the node
2) cluster ip : service creates a virtual IP inside the cluster to enable the communications b/w diff pods
or b/w set of frontend pods and backend pods
3) load balancer : it provisions a load balancer for our application in supported cloud providers

Node Port Kubernetes service:

pod will be having a network namespace and along with that a pod will have IP(eg: 10.244.0.2)

Target port: it is the pod port which pod is listening(eg: 80)
this is where service forwards requests to

(eg:80)Port: port on service, where service listens and forwards to Target port(pod port)

the service is like a virtual server inside the node
inside the cluster it will have its own ip address, it is called cluster IP of the service(eg: 10.106.1.12)

Node Port: Port on the node itself, which the we use to access the web server externally
Node port range(30000-32767), is available only in this range


